  "content": {
    "id": "p42-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Let $2x^3+4x^2+x-1=0$ have roots $\\alpha$, $\\beta$ and $\\gamma$. Find the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p42-q25-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma&=-\\frac{4}{2}\\\\\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma&=-2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q25-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha=\\frac{1}{2}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q25-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3$\n\nUse the square of the sum of roots minus twice the sum of pairwise products.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2&=(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)^2-2(\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2&=(-2)^2-2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2&=3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q25-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\alpha\\beta\\gamma^2+\\alpha\\beta^2\\gamma+\\alpha^2\\beta\\gamma$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1$\n\nFactor out $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma$ and use the sum of roots.",
          "worked": "The product of the roots is $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=-\\dfrac{-1}{2}=\\dfrac{1}{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha\\beta\\gamma^2+\\alpha\\beta^2\\gamma+\\alpha^2\\beta\\gamma&=\\alpha\\beta\\gamma(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)\\\\\\alpha\\beta\\gamma^2+\\alpha\\beta^2\\gamma+\\alpha^2\\beta\\gamma&=\\frac{1}{2}(-2)\\\\\\alpha\\beta\\gamma^2+\\alpha\\beta^2\\gamma+\\alpha^2\\beta\\gamma&=-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
